Chris Odorjan wrote:
> (Someone posted instructions on using MinGW to compile Nethack quite
> a while ago, I'm not sure how current they'd be now.)

These are the current MingW instructions:

* Download MinGW-3.1.0.exe and run it:
http://prdownloads.sf.net/mingw/MinGW-3.1.0-1.exe?download

* Download mingw32-make-3.80.0-3.exe and run it:
http://prdownloads.sf.net/mingw/mingw32-make-3.80.0-3.exe?download

* Start a CMD window.
* Add C:\Mingw\bin;c:\mingw\mingw32\bin to your path.

* Download the nethack source and unpack it.  Change to the top
directory of the nethack source (one level above src).

* Run sys\winnt\nhsetup.bat

* tweak include\config.h as you desire.  For my desire, I wanted a
version that wrote saves and bones that were binary-compatible with the
distributed nethack.exe, so I did this:
   comment out lines that #define COMPRESS,COMPRESS_EXTENSION,HACKDIR
   uncomment line that #defines AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS

* cd src

* mingw32-make -f Makefile.gcc Install



